      "message": "just a thought: wondering if we could consider NULL as a special case as a documentation for __pa implementation in kernel?:\n```\n  static inline void *kern_pkvm_va(void *va)\n  {\n  \treturn va ? __pkvm_va(__pkvm_pa(va)) : NULL;\n  }\n```\n\nI was reading the __pa implementation and it calls __phys_addr() which BUGS_ON() if va \u003d\u003d NULL when CONFIG_DEBUG_VIRTUAL enabled. But host can genuinely pass va \u003d NULL and we have check in pkvm for NULL like this eg:\n\n```\n        shared_lapic_regs \u003d kern_pkvm_va(READ_ONCE(shared_apic-\u003eregs));\n        if (!shared_lapic_regs) {\n                ret \u003d -EINVAL;\n                goto unshare_apic;\n        }\n```\n\nThis could panic when CONFIG_DEBUG_VIRTUAL enabled.\n\nBut we disable CONFIG_DEBUG_VIRTUAL in undef.h so not an issue at all for us right now.",
